  "definition": "A comprehensive governance framework \u2014 popularised by Gartner and aligned with the NIST AI Risk Management Framework \u2014 for managing the trustworthiness, security, and ethical risks of AI systems throughout their lifecycle. It operationalises three pillars: Trust (transparent, auditable, reliable AI behaviour), Risk (proactive identification and mitigation of algorithmic bias, data quality issues, and regulatory non-compliance), and Security (protection against adversarial attacks, data poisoning, and model integrity threats).",
